  "discharged": "The period map on the original Gamma0 cusp space is constructed from convergent actual integrals of f(z)P(z,1). A common holomorphic primitive and cusp limits prove geometric additivity. Homogeneous scaling and existing cusp decay derive holomorphy, convergence, and uniform strip decay for the actual integrand. The slash identities use the existing integral polynomial representation; its inverse action proves invariance, allowing descent to the actual coinvariants. The map is complex-linear and its value on each symbol is the original integral. The original Hecke-finiteness reduction now uses this constructed map, removing the separately supplied pairing premise. Positive integral matrix substitution is proved as an input to, but not a proof of, original Hecke adjointness.",
